- Congress should reject this National AI Injury Compensation Program because it solves an accountability problem by eliminating accountability — replacing the deterrent effect of direct liability with a socialized insurance scheme that lets developers externalize risk while the excise tax mechanism punishes exactly the wrong actors and shields exactly the wrong behavior.
- The compensation program does not fix information asymmetry — it institutionalizes it by replacing adversarial litigation, where plaintiffs can demand discovery and expert testimony, with an administrative claims process where the government decides what harms qualify for compensation based on criteria that AI companies will inevitably help write.
